From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:19:40 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: macaudio: add the J616s headphone jack card

On the J616s the jack's CS42L84 sits on a different AOP firmware
stream than the speaker amps, with a different frame: the jack's
stream on MCA cluster 2 is a 64-SCLK frame with a one-SCLK FSYNC
pulse, two 32-bit slots and data launched on the rising SCLK edge,
which is DSP_A with an inverted bit clock (as on the J700), while the
amps take I2S with an inverted frame clock on a 250-SCLK frame.

Give the jack a card of its own, "apple,j616-macaudio-jack": the AOP
audio driver's jack component provides its front-ends
(j616-jack-pcm-0 and -1) and back-end, and the primary front-end's
64 bit-clock ratio gives the codec its 3.072 MHz. A card binds only
once all of its codecs have probed, so as a link of the speaker card
a codec that never answers would take the speakers down with it; on
its own card it costs the jack only. Like the speaker card, it takes
the front-ends' CPU component as their PCM provider, since the AOP
speaker and jack components share one OF node.

The jack component has no PCM2, so the fixed route PCM2 RX <- Speaker
Sense Capture fails and the card does not register:

  snd-soc-macaudio sound-jack: ASoC: Failed to add route Speaker Sense Capture -> PCM2 RX(*)

Drop the route whenever the sense link is dropped. Cards with MCA
front-ends lose a route to an unused widget.

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit 89e37ed97a633b82b4ae5e621d3a0318d00eeb9f)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c b/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
index c3a646d6d4..32561ba627 100644
--- a/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
+++ b/sound/soc/apple/macaudio.c
@@ -2010,6 +2010,22 @@ struct macaudio_platform_cfg macaudio_j616_cfg = {
 	.fe_cpu_is_platform = true,
 };
 
+/*
+ * The J616s headphone jack, a card of its own: a CS42L84 on the AOP's
+ * "jack" back-end, which the firmware runs on MCA cluster 2 as a 64-SCLK
+ * frame at 48 kHz (3.072 MHz, the primary front-end's ratio) with a
+ * one-SCLK FSYNC pulse, two 32-bit slots and data launched on the rising
+ * SCLK edge: DSP_A with an inverted bit clock, as on the J700. A card binds
+ * only once all of its codecs have probed; apart from the speaker card, a
+ * codec that never answers costs the jack only. The second front-end only
+ * satisfies the fixed routes: the AOP component refuses to open it.
+ */
+struct macaudio_platform_cfg macaudio_j616_jack_cfg = {
+	.fe_dai_names = { "j616-jack-pcm-0", "j616-jack-pcm-1" },
+	.dai_fmt = SND_SOC_DAIFMT_DSP_A | SND_SOC_DAIFMT_CBC_CFC | SND_SOC_DAIFMT_IB_NF,
+	.fe_cpu_is_platform = true,
+};
+
 struct macaudio_platform_cfg macaudio_fallback_cfg = {
 	false,	AMP_NONE,	SPKR_NONE,	false,	0,	0,
 };
@@ -2071,6 +2087,8 @@ static const struct of_device_id macaudio_snd_device_id[]  = {
 	/* j615    AID21   sn012776    15      2x 2W+1T Compat: apple,j415-macaudio */
 	/* j616    AID35   sn012776    15      2x 2W+1T (AOP-fed, one serializer) */
 	{ .compatible = "apple,j616-macaudio", .data = &macaudio_j616_cfg },
+	/* j616    AID35   cs42l84     -       the jack, a card of its own (AOP-fed) */
+	{ .compatible = "apple,j616-macaudio-jack", .data = &macaudio_j616_jack_cfg },
 	/* j700    AID44   max98360a   -       2x 1W    (AOP-fed, software gain) */
 	{ .compatible = "apple,j700-macaudio", .data = &macaudio_j700_cfg },
 	/* Fallback, jack only */
@@ -2127,6 +2145,14 @@ static int macaudio_snd_platform_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * Without sense the PCM2 link is gone, and a card whose front-ends
+	 * are not the MCA's (the J616 jack) has no PCM2 RX widget at all.
+	 * The sense route is the table's last entry.
+	 */
+	if (!data->has_sense)
+		card->num_dapm_routes--;
+
 	/* Remove useless controls */
 	if (!data->has_speakers) /* No speakers, remove both */
 		card->num_controls -= MACAUDIO_NUM_SPEAKER_CONTROLS;
